<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador bank liquidity falls 0.09 pct by April 4.</title>
<headline>Ecuador bank liquidity falls 0.09 pct by April 4.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's Central Bank said Tuesday liquidity in the banking system fell 0.09 percent or 18 million sucres to 19.13 billion sucres in the week to April 18.</p>
<p>At the end of March, bank liquidity stood at 18.37 billion sucres.</p>
<p>Total liquidity in the bank sector ended 1996 at 16.99 billion sucres, up 35.8 percent from 1995.</p>
<p>((--Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433))</p>
